            <ArticleTitle>Improving patient moving and handling skills.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-6, 109-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Training in manual handling should incorporate a problem-solving approach. The handling and moving of patients is a learned skill that needs regular revision. Assessment of patient capabilities is essential, as is the provision of a safe, ergonomically satisfactory environment. There is no single technique that works in all situations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
